From 319c4bdbf89d2bc12a2648678acad7b9bf727a20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:48:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Bluetooth: MGMT: finish a mesh transmission that ends
 while powered off

mesh_send_done() queues mesh_send_done_sync() with hci_cmd_sync_queue(),
which returns -ENETDOWN once the device is closed. If the controller is
powered off after a mesh packet was started and before its done work
runs, that work is never queued, and nothing else completes the request
or clears HCI_MESH_SENDING: power off does not touch hdev->mesh_pending
and the flag is not volatile. After the controller is powered on again
every Mesh Send is acknowledged and queued behind the stale flag, none
is ever started, and Read Mesh Features keeps listing the old handles
until the controller is removed.

Queue the done work with hci_cmd_sync_submit(), which does not check
HCI_RUNNING, so that it still runs while the device is down: its
tear-down commands fail on the closed device, the request that owned
the instance is completed, and mesh_next() completes the requests that
are still pending, since no start can be queued, and clears the flag.
hci_cmd_sync_submit() still refuses new work once the device is being
unregistered.

Fixes: b338d91703fa ("Bluetooth: Implement support for Mesh")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/mgmt.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
index a8a9fda75dae..f73cd5b85c09 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
@@ -1167,7 +1167,12 @@ static void mesh_send_done(struct work_struct *work)
 	if (!hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_MESH_SENDING))
 		return;
 
-	hci_cmd_sync_queue(hdev, mesh_send_done_sync, NULL, NULL);
+	/* Not hci_cmd_sync_queue(), which fails while the device is down:
+	 * a transmission whose interval ends after a power off still has to
+	 * be accounted for and handed over, or HCI_MESH_SENDING stays set
+	 * and no later request is ever started.
+	 */
+	hci_cmd_sync_submit(hdev, mesh_send_done_sync, NULL, NULL);
 }
 
 static void mgmt_init_hdev(struct sock *sk, struct hci_dev *hdev)
-- 
